# L §6.4, §8.3 (tally 2.1.7 B7, issue #103; pre-M1 P14): a scenario's move over an open index whose instances fall
# before its from: load never sees an open index's keys, so it doesn't see the instances exist; they are left out
# at run, with no refusal. 2.1.6's refcore refused the scenario LOAD-SCENARIO. (T's S kernel g6/scen_open.)
=== scen_open_base.tally
model g6_scen_open
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, pre-M1 (#97, chunk 4, #103, P14): the base of scenario s, which declares a move over the months and an open index acct whose instances fall before its from, 1 June (L §6.4, A-9; §8.3): load never sees an open index's keys, so it can't see that these instances exist; they are left out at run, not refused LOAD-SCENARIO. Held for #103: refcore refuses the scenario. g6/scen_early is its twin over the days"

source card "a card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index month = month 2026-01..2026-12

index acct: open

kind pays: transfers

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input lim[k in acct]: money PLN

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  lim[x1] = 10.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask a: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
=== scen_open.tally
scenario s over g6_scen_open
  tally 2
  from 2026-06-01

move topup[d in month, k in acct]: pays
  on start_of(d)
  leg cash from world to konto amount lim[k]

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-12-31) in s
=== expect
a: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
b: 170.00 PLN
  world: s
  left out: topup, 5 instances, first 2026-01-01
  cut 2026-01-01
